# Stamp content dates on staged Markdown/MDX edits, then re-stage
# the files the script touched (new dateCreated / datePublished /
# dateModified values belong in the same commit as the edit).
#
# The script only touches files whose body changed against HEAD, so a
# commit with no content edits is a no-op. Note: `git add` stages the
# whole touched file — if a content file has unstaged hunks you meant
# to keep out of this commit, unstage them after this hook runs.
node scripts/manage-content-dates.mjs --stage
